window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>She has two things: a haunted lighthouse and the worst cat in the world.</b></p> <p>Pennywise is a cat only a doting owner could love, but Bernie brings him with her anyway when she runs to the edge of the world—or at least the edge of the North American continent. Heartbroken and grieving, she finds a lighthouse to live in and a quiet, secluded fishing town to call her own.</p> <p>All she wants is to be left alone with her horrible demon cat.</p> <p>But her lighthouse appears to be haunted, someone is trying to kill her, and the most gorgeous guy she's ever seen just walked into her world.</p> <p>He only wants something to call his own.</p> <p>Big, burly, gruff bear shifter Tor is a born protector who has spent his life taking care of his rowdy, unruly family. But what he truly craves is a den and a mate of his own.</p> <p>Then a beautiful, wounded woman moves into the lighthouse on the point.</p> <p>The moment Tor lays eyes on her, he knows that she's his fated mate.</p> <p>And he would do anything to keep her safe—whether that's unmasking a killer, solving a ghostly mystery, or even learning to love her truly unbearable cat.</p> <p><i>This is a steamy, funny, full-length paranormal shifter novel with a guaranteed HEA!</i></p> <p><i>Jump into a cozy, spicy paranormal romance series featuring a magical shifter town, a sexy, protective hero with a chaotic polar bear family, a tough heroine picking up the pieces of her shattered heart, a maybe-haunted lighthouse... and a cat only his owner could love.</i></p>"; 
